I'm not a lawyer, but my Dad wanted me to be one, so this cannot be 
interpreted as legal advice...

===================================BEGIN================================
The Canadian Constitution, the Canada Act of 1981 says (in part):

Fundamental Freedoms

2. Everyone has the following fundamental freedoms:

(b) freedom of thought, belief, opinion and expression, including freedom
of the press and other media of communication

(d) freedom of association.

Application of Charter

33.(1)Parliament or the legislature of a province may expressly declare in
an Act of Parliament or of the legislature, as the case may be, that the
Act or a provision thereof shall operate notwithstanding a provision included
in Section 2 or Section 7 to 15 of this Charter.
====================================END=================================

As you can see, the government giveth and the government taketh away.
Yes, we Canadians _have_ constitutional protection of freedom of expression
PROVIDED that Parliament or a provincial legislature decides that we don't.


> In theory a user could set up a remailer, without us knowing it. By our
