threatened or even closed down because the operators didn't sufficiently
police what their users were posting/uploading.  This seems to have produced
a large "chill" in the public BBS community about protecting individual
privacy and the right to free expression.  Most bulletin boards have had
to institute much tighter controls about what they allow to be made 
available to their clientele as a result.

